{"id":"256a095d7318cb9c","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-model-companion-uniqueness.md","title":"Uniqueness of a Model Companion up to Equivalence","display":"thm-model-companion-uniqueness — Uniqueness of a Model Companion up to Equivalence","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-model-companion-uniqueness","aliases":["17-thm-model-companion-uniqueness"],"display":"thm-model-companion-uniqueness — Uniqueness of a Model Companion up to Equivalence","depends_on":["[[17-df-model-companion]]","[[17-df-model]]","[[17-lem-universal-consequences-extension]]","[[17-thm-elementary-chain-union]]"],"label_origin":"local-descriptive-label","source_section":"3.5","source_result":"Proposition 3.5.13","source_pages_print":[198],"source_pages_djvu":[214],"source_verification":"statement and alternating elementary-chain proof compared in supplied DjVu OCR; local extension to inconsistent theories disclosed","verification_date":"2026-10-13"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-model-companion-uniqueness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-model-companion-uniqueness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-model-companion-uniqueness — Uniqueness of a Model Companion up to Equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f89b3dbb5152ec03\" href=\"?note=f89b3dbb5152ec03\" title=\"17-df-model-companion\">17-df-model-companion</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"abf539a1037d08d1\" href=\"?note=abf539a1037d08d1\" title=\"17-lem-universal-consequences-extension\">17-lem-universal-consequences-extension</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"288977f8607c0661\" href=\"?note=288977f8607c0661\" title=\"17-thm-elementary-chain-union\">17-thm-elementary-chain-union</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-descriptive-label"},{"key":"source_section","html":"3.5"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Proposition 3.5.13"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>198</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>214</span></div>"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"statement and alternating elementary-chain proof compared in supplied DjVu OCR; local extension to inconsistent theories disclosed"},{"key":"verification_date","html":"2026-10-13"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> 固定，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,T^*,T^{**}\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T,T^*,T^{**}\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>。\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f89b3dbb5152ec03\" href=\"?note=f89b3dbb5152ec03\" title=\"17-df-model-companion\">17-df-model-companion</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>。\n证明使用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"abf539a1037d08d1\" href=\"?note=abf539a1037d08d1\" title=\"17-lem-universal-consequences-extension\">17-lem-universal-consequences-extension</a> 的延拓及 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"288977f8607c0661\" href=\"?note=288977f8607c0661\" title=\"17-thm-elementary-chain-union\">17-thm-elementary-chain-union</a> 的初等链定理。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\bigl(\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L(T^*,T)\\land\n\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L(T^{**},T)\\bigr)\n\\ \\longrightarrow\\\n\\operatorname{Mod}(T^*)=\\operatorname{Mod}(T^{**}).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\bigl(\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L(T^*,T)\\land\n\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L(T^{**},T)\\bigr)\n\\ \\longrightarrow\\\n\\operatorname{Mod}(T^*)=\\operatorname{Mod}(T^{**}).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书 Proposition 3.5.13，印刷 p.198、DjVu 214，陈述及交替链证明已对照 OCR。</p>\n<p>从任意 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^*\">\\(T^*\\)</span> 的模型出发，共全称后承允许依次嵌入 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^{**}\">\\(T^{**}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^*\">\\(T^*\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^{**}\">\\(T^{**}\\)</span> 的模型；经同构替换可取实际递增链。奇数项之间的包含在 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^*\">\\(T^*\\)</span> 的模型完全性下是初等的，偶数项同理。两个子链有同一个并，初等链定理使并成为两边首项的初等扩张。因此首项也满足另一理论。交换两理论即得模型类相等。</p>\n<p>唯一性是逻辑等价意义的唯一性，不能把结论加强为公理集合字面相等。</p>\n<p>一致性约定：原书印刷 p.186（DjVu 202）的模型完全性定义限于一致理论；本条沿用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"59d623a1692279f1\" href=\"?note=59d623a1692279f1\" title=\"17-df-model-completeness\">17-df-model-completeness</a> 的本地谓词，保留不一致时的空真延拓。故来源对应在一致理论上按原书理解；不一致边界由模型类为空另行核对，不把该延拓冒称原书定义。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-model-companion","status":"resolved","id":"f89b3dbb5152ec03","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-model-companion]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","head